alysis, Office of Nuclear Regulatory Research, U.S. Nuclear Regulatory Commission,cApril 2026.  a1 online resource.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aInternational Agreement Report ;vNUREG/IA-0559  a"A. Hsieh, NRC project manager."  aTechnical;bApril 2026 0aNuclear power plantsxPiping.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85093048 0aNuclear reactorsxComputer simulation. 0aWater hammerxMathematical models. 0aTwo-phase flowxMathematical models. 0aNuclear energy.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85092958 7aNuclear energy.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01039951 0aInternational agreement report ;vNUREG/IA-0559.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8672909140uhttps://purl.fdlp.gov/GPO/gpo255443704 zAddress at time of PURL creationuhttps://www.nrc.gov/docs/ML2611/ML26112A178.pdf  aC0bGPO  abcs87 20260429b20260429  abc34 20261022b20261022  aUNREPORTEDPUBSSTAFFb20260429  aBIBCONEWb20261022  aCATLEVELBASICb20260429  aPERM_INGEST_06012026  aVEND01b2026102803719cam a2200565 i 00147189720261001131823.0m     o  d f      cr |||||||||||260116s2025    aluab   ob   f000 0 eng c  a(OCoLC)1569075950  aAAUbengerdaepncAAUdOCLCOdGPO  apcc  aa-cc---aa-ii---  aXZL4  a0422-K (online)0 aD 301.26/6:T 43/21 aVan Oudenaren, John,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8112364610aRemote basing :bPeople's Liberation Army logistics on the Tibetan Plateau /cprepared by BluePath Labs ; John S. Van Oudenaren.30aPeople's Liberation Army logistics on the Tibetan Plateau3 aPLA's logistics on the Tibetan Plateau 1aMontgomery, AL :bChina Aerospace Studies Institute,c2025.  a1 online resource (57 pages) :bcolor illustrations, color maps  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  atextbPDF2rdaft  a"November 2025."  aThis is a publication issued by the United States federal government or produced with federal funds.  aIn scope of the U.S. Government Publishing Office Cataloging and Indexing Program (C&I) and Federal Depository Library Program (FDLP).  aIncludes bibliographical references (pages 43-57).0 aIntroduction -- PLA force structure and logistical support in Tibet -- Remote basing: Logistical support methods.  a"The People's Liberation Army (PLA) is at the forefront of China's efforts to defend its extensive land border with India and maintain firm control over Tibet. As both China and India have expanded their respective infrastructural and military basing networks along the Line of Actual Control (the sectors of the Sino-Indian border where demarcation remains disputed), significant escalations have occurred, most notably the Doklam Standoff in mid-2017 and the Galwan Valley skirmish in June 2020. For the PLA, providing logistical support and sustainment to troops stationed on the "roof of the world" is a longstanding challenge. Nevertheless, despite the generally difficult geography on the Chinese side of the border, more effective logistical support appears to remain an enduring advantage for the PLA over the Indian Armed Forces."--Publisher's description.  aDescription based on online resource; title from PDF cover (airuniversity.af.edu, viewed April 16, 2026).10aChina.bZhongguo ren min jie fang junxProcurement. 0aMilitary baseszTibetan Plateau. 0aChinaxForeign relationszIndia. 0aIndiaxForeign relationszChina. 6aChine0(CaQQLa)201-0053864xRelations extérieures0(CaQQLa)201-0053864zInde.0(CaQQLa)201-0482676 6aInde0(CaQQLa)201-0156737xRelations extérieures0(CaQQLa)201-0156737zChine.0(CaQQLa)201-04766192 aChina Aerospace Studies Institute (U.S.),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20170137452 aBluePath Labs (Firm)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no202304439140uhttps://purl.fdlp.gov/GPO/gpo255294704 zAddress at time of PURL creationuhttps://www.airuniversity.af.edu/Porta